Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.27,0:00:06.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was the stone, as red as blood,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.63,0:00:11.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,which promised to turn suffering to delight, bring victory to battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.38,0:00:13.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and life back to the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.20,0:00:19.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In reverence, people referred to it \Nas "The Philosopher's Stone."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.37,0:00:37.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can this be possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.99,0:00:39.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.61,0:00:44.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the answer we finally arrive at \Nafter seeking it for so long?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.62,0:00:49.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can living people be the ingredients for a Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.76,0:00:51.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so many of them, to boot!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.16,0:00:57.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.90,0:01:01.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.18,0:01:06.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.91,0:01:12.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.25,0:02:50.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,M-Major, p-please, wait a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.42,0:02:51.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.31,0:02:58.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, right now, they appear to be tired, so we probably shouldn't disturb them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.44,0:03:00.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? They're tired?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.70,0:03:04.23,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,In that case, I'll invite them to have dinner, \Nwhich will invigorate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.23,0:03:05.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, no! Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.61,0:03:08.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, the two of them are resting.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.94,0:03:12.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will tell them that \Nyou came by, Major.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.28,0:03:16.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. I guess there's nothing I can do if they're sleeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.92,0:03:45.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,God must really hate people who have committed taboo.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.60,0:03:51.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just when we think things are \Nwithin reach, they run away from us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.19,0:03:53.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it repeats.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.92,0:04:00.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And when they're finally within our grasp, we get kicked down by them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.99,0:04:07.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this going to happen \Nfor our whole lives?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.99,0:04:08.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.65,0:04:13.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought that once we found the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.98,0:04:16.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,our wish would be granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.83,0:04:21.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll find it, that's for sure! \NAfter all, we're trying this hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.03,0:04:22.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They may say that you're a dog of the military
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.79,0:04:25.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that you've sold your soul \Nfor special privileges,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.25,0:04:27.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but haven't we persevered without admitting defeat?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.09,0:04:29.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.42,0:04:32.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, we'll find it for sure, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.07,0:04:56.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.35,0:05:00.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's try starting from square one again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.32,0:05:02.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.56,0:05:06.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a chance that \Nwe misread something.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.73,0:05:08.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I said I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.77,0:05:13.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what if we try re-reading it? \NWe might discover something new!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.10,0:05:16.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to give it a shot. Let's keep trying!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.50,0:05:18.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you, I've had enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.59,0:05:35.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.72,0:05:39.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.05,0:05:50.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. I don't even \Nwant to look at it anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.24,0:05:52.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.65,0:06:03.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, that's it, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.96,0:06:08.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You won't regret \Nhaving given up here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.03,0:06:17.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is what you've been searching for something you would abandon this easily?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.23,0:06:21.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop going on when you \Ndon't even know the half of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.68,0:06:29.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know. I know that you guys are seeking the Philosopher's Stone
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.64,0:06:33.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that it is made by \Nsacrificing living people.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.47,0:06:38.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew it was rude, \Nbut I allowed myself to listen in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.09,0:06:42.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you've listened in, \Nthen you must know
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.13,0:06:45.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that it won't do any good to investigate any further. Just leave us alone!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.79,0:06:50.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really are a child, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.03,0:06:55.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're scared, right? \NThat the answers might disappear?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.96,0:07:00.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't want to acknowledge that everything you've gone through this far
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.38,0:07:01.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,might be in vain, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.72,0:07:05.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Am I wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.96,0:07:18.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't it okay if it doesn't \Nmean anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.57,0:07:27.30,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Verifying whether or not this means anything is worth something, if you ask me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.74,0:07:31.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What you're seeking isn't \Nanything all that simple, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.81,0:07:36.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you keep trying \Na little longer, Edward-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.01,0:07:49.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.93,0:07:51.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though the answers are going to change
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.95,0:07:53.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,just because I chuck it \Nall along the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.50,0:07:55.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.52,0:08:00.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've come this far! \NHow can we end it all halfway?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.07,0:08:01.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to \Nsee it to the end!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.43,0:08:03.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's do it, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.68,0:08:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.92,0:08:12.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san's research is sound in theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.74,0:08:16.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, it still didn't result in a perfect Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.37,0:08:18.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There still might be other possibilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.43,0:08:23.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I'm going to verify the truth of Marcoh-san's theory with my own eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.63,0:08:25.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.11,0:08:33.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The genuine truth behind truths...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.30,0:08:37.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Behind... truths...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.38,0:08:40.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it! There's something else!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.22,0:08:44.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to this data,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.92,0:08:48.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a considerably large facility would be needed to create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.31,0:08:53.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are currently four alchemy laboratories under the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.72,0:08:59.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Among those, Doctor Marcoh was assigned to the 3rd Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.22,0:09:02.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I went around to all of the laboratories in the city,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.63,0:09:05.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and there wasn't any research \Nall that remarkable going on there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.90,0:09:07.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.27,0:09:11.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, in the past, \Nthat was the 5th laboratory,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.74,0:09:13.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but it was closed down, \Nand is deserted now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.53,0:09:17.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a risk of it collapsing, so it was made off-limits.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.07,0:09:18.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's there!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.07,0:09:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.82,0:09:23.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a prison next to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.69,0:09:26.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central 2nd Prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.12,0:09:27.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.66,0:09:30.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With people being the ingredient for a Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.54,0:09:34.42,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,what if they did their research there because it was the easiest place to procure them?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.42,0:09:37.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean, they used prisoners?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.18,0:09:38.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.58,0:09:40.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they didn't execute \Ncondemned criminals
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.20,0:09:43.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and instead used them as live materials, that would explain it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.59,0:09:44.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's in charge of \Nthe laboratories?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.02,0:09:49.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That would have been \NBrig. Gen. Basque Grand.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.91,0:09:52.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he was killed by Scar \Nsome time ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.95,0:09:57.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.53,0:09:58.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've got no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.43,0:10:01.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How about we check things out directly?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.23,0:10:01.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.79,0:10:03.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,J-Just a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.99,0:10:06.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From here on, \Nthis is grown-ups' work.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.16,0:10:08.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, Scar is still after you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.75,0:10:11.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's too dangerous for you \Nto go walking around outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.05,0:10:12.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but still...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.98,0:10:17.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We will investigate the 5th Laboratory. You wait here, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.72,0:10:20.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we learn anything, \Nwe will report it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.16,0:10:22.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you please...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.56,0:10:25.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.40,0:10:33.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So be it. Okay, it's up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.13,0:10:36.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll ask you to handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.95,0:10:38.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right! Leave it to us!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.19,0:11:13.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel Hughes,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.79,0:11:18.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm finished writing down the \Ncourt record for case number 3263.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.09,0:11:22.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, is that right? \NSorry, hang on a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.59,0:11:27.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, let's have you continue on with case number 9572, if you would.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.04,0:11:31.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're going to use it in a trial tomorrow, so put a rush on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.38,0:11:33.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.42,0:11:35.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?! Are you tired?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.28,0:11:36.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, not particularly!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.13,0:11:41.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look here! This one is \Na special swimsuit version!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.60,0:11:44.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think? \NShe's so cute, it just melts your heart!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.74,0:11:48.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just looking at this, the fatigue just flies away, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.08,0:11:50.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How about it? Hm? Hm?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.58,0:11:53.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.38,0:11:55.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It does, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.31,0:11:56.48,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Um, Lt. Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.13,0:11:58.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My daughter is such a little healer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.48,0:11:58.74,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel! What is the problem there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.80,0:12:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, did you find Scar's body?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.45,0:12:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not yet, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.95,0:12:07.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right. As for the matter of us sending security to the library,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.91,0:12:09.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,hurry and take care of that for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.59,0:12:14.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, I've been introduced to quite a find here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.86,0:12:16.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I owe one to Ed for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.81,0:12:37.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tripwire alarms?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.55,0:12:41.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For a building that isn't being used, the security sure is tight, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.44,0:12:42.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is getting more \Nand more suspicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.05,0:12:44.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right, let's go around back.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.16,0:12:53.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.40,0:12:56.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ups-a-daisy!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.03,0:13:02.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hate to say it, \Nbut it's times like this
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.65,0:13:05.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that I'm glad I don't have my flesh-and-blood arm and leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.55,0:13:07.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Same here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.98,0:13:17.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This entrance is locked up tight, too, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.71,0:13:19.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, over there...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.15,0:13:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like it goes \Nall the way inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.37,0:13:29.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, you wait here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.91,0:13:31.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Will you be all right \Nby yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.91,0:13:36.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right or not, your huge size won't fit through here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.08,0:13:38.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, I'll be back in a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.30,0:13:42.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not this big \Nbecause I wanted to be!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.09,0:13:45.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is Lt. Maria Ross.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.96,0:13:48.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.08,0:13:51.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.36,0:13:53.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major, I need to talk to you \Nabout something.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.69,0:14:04.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.69,0:14:07.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Contact the Command Center at once, \Nand call in reinforcements!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.34,0:14:08.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.28,0:14:18.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have no business with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.99,0:14:21.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is Fullmetal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.27,0:14:36.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Two of you stay here! \NWe're going up another stairway!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.45,0:14:38.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's going up to Edward-san's room!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.81,0:15:17.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So Fullmetal knew about this too?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.14,0:15:29.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't move, Scar!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.21,0:15:38.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.36,0:15:40.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are Edward-san \Nand his brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.95,0:15:42.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.04,0:15:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.92,0:15:52.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town of Liore...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.62,0:15:55.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,has been dealt with \Nall neat and tidy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.12,0:15:58.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no longer anyone there who knows too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.22,0:16:00.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't say. Nice work, Envy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.11,0:16:03.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things are going well here too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.52,0:16:07.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal pipsqueak has caught wind of the laboratory, hasn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.34,0:16:11.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we dispose of him \Nbefore it gets out to the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.74,0:16:13.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to kill him, \Nlet me do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.20,0:16:18.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on. That boy might just grant us what we want.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.00,0:16:22.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we're going to kill him, it won't be too late to do so after that, will it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.44,0:16:26.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, it's fine with me as long as it doesn't throw a wrench in the works.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.76,0:16:30.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Although, it seems doubtful that \Nhe would ever arrive there safely.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.18,0:16:36.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told them not to lay a hand on those two, but it is concerning.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.59,0:16:38.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They {\i1}are{\i0} idiots, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.26,0:16:41.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it looks to be too troublesome, dispose of the whole lot of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.10,0:16:42.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.06,0:16:47.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn, this is narrower than I thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.27,0:16:51.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn it all, if I were normal-sized, \NI wouldn't have gotten through here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.95,0:16:54.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a good thing I'm so little.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.39,0:16:58.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Augh! No, it's not!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.48,0:17:09.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The lights are on...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.15,0:17:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So they're not currently using it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.30,0:17:14.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bingo!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.24,0:17:24.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What the?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.65,0:17:47.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For them to go this far, they must really not want anyone getting close.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.79,0:17:51.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds interesting! \NI'll take them on!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.92,0:18:26.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey! Aren't we under orders not to lay a hand on them?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.41,0:18:32.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care about that. \NI can't rest until I've carved them up!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.42,0:18:35.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait! There are two in our quarry. There are also two of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.48,0:18:38.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't allow you to \Nhave them all to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.93,0:18:44.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit! This thing is relentless for being just a ball!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.59,0:19:01.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It really is a good thing \NI'm so small...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.07,0:19:03.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you! This is a pain!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.48,0:19:27.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on in, they're saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.58,0:19:42.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice of you to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.61,0:19:44.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I welcome you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.95,0:19:54.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't look very welcoming.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.35,0:19:57.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am he who was entrusted to guard this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.18,0:20:01.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For the time being, \Nyou may call me Number 48.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.06,0:20:02.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Number 48?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.65,0:20:06.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been so long. I'm delighted to be able to go against someone so capable.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.65,0:20:09.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have run out of luck \Nby coming up against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.24,0:20:12.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not think ill of me, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.12,0:20:19.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And you, don't think ill of me for being the kid who defeated you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.56,0:20:24.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother sure is taking long. What could he be doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.41,0:20:35.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice. You move well for your size. \NThat's more like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.89,0:20:36.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.88,0:20:39.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should respond when asked who I am, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.52,0:20:45.68,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,My name is Number 66. \NAlthough, that's just what they call me at work.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.00,0:20:47.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Number 66?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.63,0:20:50.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I do have my own, proper name as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.43,0:20:52.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but if you heard it, you'd be \Nso surprised you'd wet yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.89,0:20:55.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll tell you when I finish you off.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.40,0:20:58.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You say you guard this place, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.60,0:21:00.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a little something I'd like to ask you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.11,0:21:03.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you can defeat me, \NI will tell you anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.91,0:21:06.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.66,0:21:07.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see how good you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.62,0:21:08.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.87,0:21:13.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your false arm is steel up to \Nthe shoulder, is it? Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.13,0:21:16.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,my beloved sword will pierce even steel!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.63,0:21:18.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've gotta be kidding!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.10,0:21:20.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I bust it again, \NWinry's gonna kill me, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.44,0:21:29.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.60,0:21:34.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oops...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.32,0:21:43.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His reflexes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.16,0:21:45.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.72,0:21:50.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.46,0:21:58.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.13,0:22:03.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.38,0:22:10.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the same kind of \Narmored body as Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.40,0:23:40.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.40,0:23:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 20: "Soul of the Guardian"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.75,0:23:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've cried a lot, laughed a lot, \Nand seen hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.07,0:23:52.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These memories are not false. \NI am human!
